{"repositoryId":1402196986,"availability":"available","full":"stuffbucket/gliner-runner","name":"gliner-runner","description":"Cross-platform GLiNER inference runner with schema-aware batching and Apple Silicon acceleration","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-02T18:24:14Z","updated":"2026-10-19T22:09:02Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://stuffbucket.github.io/gliner-runner/","topics":[],"demo":"https://stuffbucket.github.io/gliner-runner/playground/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T22:20:21.862Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T22:20:21.862Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T22:20:21.862Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-19T22:20:21.862Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["GLiNER Runner sorts text into labels you choose. It runs on your own computer, and your text never leaves it.","GLiNER Runner is a local, backend-neutral runtime and HTTP service for explicit, reproducible GLiNER inference. It implements constrained classification with the three published Fastino GLiNER2.5 Decide models, each pinned to an exact revision. There are two runners behind one HTTP protocol: the Python-free ONNX runner that Homebrew and the installer provide (the gliner-runner command used above; the original name gliner-runner-onnx also works), and a Python server that uses Fastino GLiNER2 2.1's public PyTorch Classifier.batchclassify API as the correctness oracle."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/stuffbucket/gliner-runner/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"e3efcf7fd8a645469a5fc5a9b49582c49386734f5f987294266f6b65bc8838f5","extractedAt":"2026-10-19T22:20:21.947Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T22:20:21.947Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"GLiNER Runner sorts text into labels you choose. It runs on your own computer, and your text never leaves it.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/stuffbucket/gliner-run